==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|en|kindergarden}} {{qual|misspelling}}

===Etymology===
{{ubor|en|de|Kindergarten|lit=garden of children||kindergarten}}, coined by German pedagogue Friedrich Fröbel (early 19th century).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɪndəɹˌɡɑːɹt(ə)n/|/ˈkɪndəɹˌɡɑːɹd(ə)n/|[ˈkʰɪn(d)əɹˌɡɑːɹt̬(ə)n]|[ˈkʰɪɾ̃əɹˌɡɑːɹʔn̩]|a=US,CA}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkɪndəˌɡɑːt(ə)n/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-kindergarten.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɑː(ɹ)tən|s=4}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|+|kindergärten|pl2qual=obsolete}}

# {{lb|en|North America|Australia}} An educational institution for young children, usually between ages 4 and 6; [[nursery school]]. {{defdate|from 1852}}
# {{lb|en|North America|Australia}} The [[elementary school]] [[grade]] before [[first grade]].
# {{lb|en|Philippines}} The two levels between [[nursery]] and [[prep]]; the second and third years of [[preschool]].

